--- v5/README.md
+++ v6/README.md
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # NativeGsTextFootprint (N9c)
 
-Development-only AutoCAD 2020 / R23.1 x64 ARX. `BCE_TEST_RUN` synchronously creates an owned in-memory database, one persistent point control, one 2D GS kernel/model/offscreen device/view. No working/current database switch, GUI view, DWG save, shared GS/profile modification, Plot, Python, or external converter occurs in the native command.
+Development-only AutoCAD 2020 / R23.1 x64 ARX. `BCE_TEST_RUN` synchronously creates an owned in-memory database, one persistent point control, one k3DDrawing GS kernel/model/offscreen device/view. The owned view is explicitly k3DWireframe with an orthographic XY camera; the kernel request follows the local 2020 SDK ARXDBG sample. There is one fixed request and no fallback loop. No working/current database switch, GUI view, DWG save, shared GS/profile modification, Plot, Python, or external converter occurs in the native command.
 
 The candidate uses `createAutoCADModel` and `kernel.associate(ownedDb, model, kMain)`; the association is only an attempted route. Every genuine WorldDraw independently records and checks its context database, entity database/ObjectId and model binding before drawing. An actual mismatch fails and is preserved in `gs-trace.jsonl`; it does not establish impossibility of other public routes.
 
